{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 41, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Mark stood bolt upright in his unnaturally perfect bed, the comforter impeccably smooth like a character’s model. His fingers trembled as he lifted his phone—still at 100% battery, the time stuck on 3:33 AM, a number that felt like a joke. The digital clock flickered once, then reset itself. He pinched his arm; no pain, no blood—just the same polished skin he’d woken up with every morning for years. Outside his window, the city blurred at the edges, textures pixelating like a glitch, and when he reached for the doorknob, the wood dissolved into a floating UI bar. His breath hitched. This wasn’t his apartment. It was a loading screen, and he was the playing character.\n\nThe world responded to his panic. Tapping the air summoned a minimap, his health bar glowing green above his head. A distant notification pinged: *\"New Quest: Identify Your Glitch.\"* Mark lunged for his dresser, fingers brushing over a non-existent wallet, a nonexistent coffee mug—objects that flickered in and out of existence. He stumbled into the hallway, where neighbors’ doors led to blank menus, their voices replaced by placeholder soundbites. A child’s laughter echoed from down the block, warped into a chiptune melody. Then, the screen stuttered. A red alert flashed: *\"ERROR: PLAYER UNRECOGNIZED. INITIATING DEBUG MODE.\"* Mark’s knees gave out. If this was a game, then who—or what—had forgotten to save him?", "logprobs": [{"token": "Mark", "logprob": -2.903310775756836}, {"token": " stood", "logprob": -3.7322187423706055}, {"token": " bolt", "logprob": -2.3335700035095215}, {"token": " upright", "logprob": -0.006865246687084436}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.14669375121593475}, {"token": " his", "logprob": -0.7075226306915283}, {"token": " un", "logprob": -2.0573573112487793}, {"token": "n", "logprob": -1.145547866821289}, {"token": "atur", "logprob": -0.0935585647